WEBVTT

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.070 line:6% position:50% align:center
lest I come and strike the land
with a decree of utter destruction.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.500 line:6% position:50% align:center
These are the last words of the Old Testament.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:19.000 line:6% position:50% align:center
In your Bible, it is just one page to the next book.
But in the 400 years between,
no new word came from heaven.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.531 line:6% position:50% align:center
People waited.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:27.901 line:6% position:50% align:center
If it seems slow, wait for it

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.817 line:6% position:50% align:center
But God had not stopped.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:40.400 line:6% position:50% align:center
The head of this image was of fine gold, its chest and arms of silver,
its middle and thighs of bronze, its legs of iron,
its feet partly of iron and partly of clay.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.840 line:6% position:50% align:center
These metals pointed to kingdoms
that would rise one after another.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:49.680 line:6% position:50% align:center
Through those 400 years,
God was preparing the world, step by step.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.028 line:6% position:50% align:center
Wherever the scattered Jewish people went,
they carried the Word with them,

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.900 line:6% position:50% align:center
After Alexander, the wide world
could talk in one common language: Greek.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:04.850 line:6% position:50% align:center
The Scriptures were translated into that language,
and even Gentiles could now read them,

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:09.163 line:6% position:50% align:center
Rome opened roads and sea lanes
to every corner of the empire.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.173 line:6% position:50% align:center
In synagogues across the empire,
the Word was read every Sabbath.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.711 line:6% position:50% align:center
This is how God prepared the way.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.428 line:6% position:50% align:center
your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son,
and you shall call his name John.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:26.850 line:6% position:50% align:center
Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.234 line:6% position:50% align:center
And he will turn the hearts of fathers to their children

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.590 line:6% position:50% align:center
in the spirit and power of Elijah,
to turn the hearts of the fathers to the children,

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:45.145 line:6% position:50% align:center
After 400 years, God spoke again.
The one to come like Elijah: John the Baptist.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:57.440 line:6% position:50% align:center
a stone was cut out by no human hand,
and it struck the image on its feet of iron and clay,
and broke them in pieces.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:01.380 line:6% position:50% align:center
But when the fullness of time had come,
God sent forth his Son,

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:05.500 line:6% position:50% align:center
The stone God sent:
his Son, Jesus, came.

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:09.302 line:6% position:50% align:center
For the Son of Man came
to seek and to save the lost.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:17.359 line:6% position:50% align:center
In the synagogue of his hometown,
Jesus unrolled the scroll of the prophet Isaiah,
written some 700 years before.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.641 line:6% position:50% align:center
Today this Scripture has been fulfilled in your hearing.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.456 line:6% position:50% align:center
The one promised some 700 years before
was Jesus himself.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:36.220 line:6% position:50% align:center
Jesus died on the cross for our sins
and was raised on the third day.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:43.226 line:6% position:50% align:center
Along those roads, Paul preached the gospel in Greek,
starting in the synagogues.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:52.611 line:6% position:50% align:center
God was at work even when he was silent.
And now, he is at work in your waiting too.
